# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.
#
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# OPERATOR DECREE 08/11/2026 — ALL IN ON GRAPHIFY HOSTED.
# Verbatim: "make everything not gitignored, we are public anyway, we only use
# graphify, no grepping."
#
# This repo is PUBLIC (verified `gh repo view` → isPrivate:false). Everything we
# WRITE is now tracked, so the hosted graph can index it — most importantly the
# 93 research documents under _RESEARCH/ that RULE 0.4 exists because nobody
# could find. A gitignored file is invisible to graphify on EVERY tier; no
# amount of paying fixes it. That is the whole reason this file shrank.
#
# EXACTLY TWO THINGS STAY IGNORED, and neither is "our content":
#   1. CREDENTIALS — publishing a live key to a public repo is permanent (git
#      history survives deletion) and forces a full rotation. Never negotiable.
#   2. MACHINE JUNK + LARGE BINARIES — dependencies, build output, caches, and
#      generated data dumps. Committing node_modules would hand the graph
#      hundreds of thousands of nodes of OTHER PEOPLE'S code and bury ours,
#      which defeats the decree rather than serving it.
# Anything that is neither a secret nor a build artifact belongs in the graph.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. CREDENTIALS — NEVER COMMIT. PUBLIC REPO. UNDOING THIS REQUIRES ROTATION.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# dlt secrets and pipeline state (never commit credentials)
/.dlt/
.dlt/secrets.toml
.dlt/.pipeline/

# Defensive glob — catches any secrets.toml anywhere in the tree
# (e.g. ingest/secrets.toml if a future dlt entry point writes outside .dlt/)
**/secrets.toml

# cloud-secrets: ONLY the encrypted vault.enc is committed. The passphrase and any
# decrypted/plaintext key material must NEVER be committed.
cloud-secrets/.passphrase
cloud-secrets/*.key

# RLS prod-probe — connects to the prod DB with a HARDCODED password on line 4.
# Operator's local-only verification tool; one `git add .` away from leaking the
# prod credential, so it must never be tracked. (Wired 2026-06-10.)
scripts/_rls_probe.py

# Certificates / private keys
*.pem

# personal_vault backups — the operator's PERSONAL strategy notes, not platform
# code. Held back from the 08/11/2026 publish decree and flagged to him in the
# same session: 2 files, 8KB, zero value to a CODE graph. Delete these three
# lines if he wants them in.
.private/


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. MACHINE JUNK, BUILD OUTPUT, LARGE BINARIES — worthless to the graph.
#    Measured 08/11/2026 before ignoring: data/ 263MB · .qmd/ 89MB ·
#    graphify-out/ 45MB · runs/ 19MB · tmp/ 6.9MB.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# dependencies
/node_modules
package-lock.json
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# third-party research clone — someone else's code; indexing it buries ours
awesome-claude-code-toolkit/

# testing
/coverage

# Playwright — scratch run output (failure screenshots/diffs); the accepted
# baselines under emails/__screenshots__/ ARE committed, this is not that.
/test-results/
/playwright-report/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# refinery (A1 lab) — raw snapshots + per-stage JSON
.refinery-cache/

# firecrawl tool cache
.firecrawl/
# Guard: a path-flattening bug can dump a .firecrawl/ output as a literal
# root-level filename (e.g. Usersethandevbrain-platform.firecrawlfiverr-data2.json),
# escaping the .firecrawl/ ignore above. Catch that shape (seen 2026-05-31).
Users*firecrawl*.json

# Python bytecode / caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Virtualenv (~1 GB on CI — the cached ingest venv restored into the workspace root)
.venv/

# JetBrains / PyCharm — per-machine project files.
.idea/
*.iml

# Local preview / proof artifacts (rendered emails, chart PNGs, scratch scripts)
tmp/

# Ingest + verification runtime logs
ingest/*.log
verification/*.log
dev-stdout.txt
dev-stderr.txt
*storybook.log
storybook-static

# Scratch / throwaway scripts and probe artifacts — regenerated, never content.
refinery/__scratch__/
__scratch__/
scripts/.prove-*
scripts/probe_*.py
scripts/deep_probe_*.py
*_probe_results.json
scripts/email/tmp-*.mts
.tmp_lb_review/

# External raw data dumps — Redfin, Zillow, etc. (263MB of CSVs/TSVs)
data/

# ALL run outputs (campaign renders, outreach previews, insiders ledgers,
# weekly-read issues) — local evidence, regenerated, never repo content.
runs/

# graphify generated output (45MB graph.json — the HOSTED index is the root of
# truth as of 08/11/2026; this local artifact is a build product, not content)
graphify-out/

# qmd hybrid-search index — machine-local (89MB sqlite)
.qmd/*.sqlite
.carousel-out/

# designlang MCP tool — local design-audit scratch output (grade cards, tokens)
design-extract-output/

# community_profiles raw-markdown fetch cache — scratch, never committed
ingest/pipelines/community_profiles/.raw_cache/

# MarketBeat / Colliers PDF drop folder — large proprietary PDFs
# Only the .gitkeep sentinel is tracked
ingest/drops/marketbeat_pdf/*.pdf

# Map build artifacts — regenerated by mapshaper from Census TIGER
public/maps/fl_zips.geojson

# Email style-gallery preview — regenerated build artifact
/style-gallery-preview.html

# dev-only email triage renders (scratch)
public/dev-emails/

# ingest-freshness map — transient per-run state, regenerated every gate run
brains/_ingest-freshness.json*

# chief-of-staff nightly working files (CI workspace + local dispatch testing)
evidence.json
chief-of-staff-brief.md

# Path-flattened Windows temp files — a script writing to %TEMP%\foo.sql lands in
# the repo root as "C:Users...foo.sql" when cwd is the repo.
*mhs_permits_inserts.sql


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. PER-MACHINE RUNTIME STATE — not secrets, not content; differs per checkout
#    and would fight other machines if tracked.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Serena MCP project memories (local, re-onboarded per-environment)
.serena/

# Claude Code per-machine permission overrides (settings.json stays shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code internal scheduler lockfile — runtime-only, per-machine
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# ephemeral Claude Code session state (tasks, notes, handoffs — not hooks/settings)
.claude/tasks/
.claude/notes/
.claude/handoffs/

# transient worktrees scaffolded by parallel-agent dispatch — never tracked
.claude/worktrees/

# session-scoped build-context intake (gated by .claude/hooks/check-build-context.mjs)
.claude/build-context.md

# Superpowers plugin runtime data — ephemeral, auto-generated per session
.superpowers/

# repolith coordination store — runtime-only per-machine claim/heartbeat/journal
.repolith/

# Hermes (local Ollama agent) per-repo context file — machine-local instructions
.hermes.md

# writ-guard-trio (08/19/2026): human-only approval tokens + hook session state - never committed
.claude/approvals/
.claude/hooks/.state/
